  m_Name: PentonTurbineData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Penton Turbine
  engineDescription: 'A Pelton Turbine is an impulse-type hydraulic turbine used
    to convert the kinetic energy of high-head, low-flow water into mechanical energy
    for electricity generation. It operates by directing high-velocity water jets
    onto specially shaped buckets mounted around the circumference of a runner, causing
    the runner to rotate. Its main components include the runner with double-cup
    buckets, nozzle, spear (needle) valve, deflector, casing, shaft, and braking
    jet. During operation, water under high pressure is discharged through the nozzle,
    where its pressure energy is converted into kinetic energy. The high-speed water
    jet strikes the buckets, transferring momentum and rotating the runner. The spent
    water is then discharged at atmospheric pressure, while the rotating shaft drives
    a generator to produce electrical power.


    Pelton turbines are widely used
    in hydroelectric power plants operating under high-head and low-flow conditions
    due to their high efficiency, simple construction, and reliable performance.'
  engineCategory: Engineering
